11-
12-BrowserFS is highly extensible, and ships with many filesystem backends:
13-
14-* `XmlHttpRequest`: Downloads files on-demand from a webserver via `XMLHttpRequest`
15-* `LocalStorage`: Stores files in the browser's `localStorage`.
16-* `HTML5FS`: Stores files into the HTML5 `FileSystem` API
17:* `IndexedDB`: Stores files into the browser's `IndexedDB` object database.
18-* `Dropbox`: Stores files into the user's Dropbox account.
19-  * Note: You provide this filesystem with an authenticated [DropboxJS client](https://github.com/dropbox/dropbox-js)
20-* `InMemory`: Stores files in-memory. Thus, it is a temporary file store that clears when the user navigates away.
21-* `ZipFS`: Read-only zip file-backed FS. Lazily decompresses files as you access them.
22-  * Supports DEFLATE out-of-the-box.
23-  * Have super old zip files? [The `browserfs-zipfs-extras` package](https://github.com/jvilk/browserfs-zipfs-extras) adds support for EXPLODE, UNREDUCE, and UNSHRINK.
24-* `IsoFS`: Mount an .iso file into the file system.
25-  * Supports Microsoft Joliet and Rock Ridge extensions to the ISO9660 standard.
26-* `WorkerFS`: Lets you mount the BrowserFS file system configured in the main thread in a WebWorker, or the other way around!
27-* `MountableFileSystem`: Lets you mount multiple file systems into a single directory hierarchy, as in *nix-based OSes.
28-* `OverlayFS`: Mount a read-only file system as read-write by overlaying a writable file system on top of it. Like Docker's overlayfs, it will only write changed files to the writable file system.
29-* `AsyncMirror`: Use an asynchronous backend synchronously. Invaluable for Emscripten; let your Emscripten applications write to larger file stores with no additional effort!
30-  * Note: Loads the entire contents of the file system into a synchronous backend during construction. Performs synchronous operations in-memory, and enqueues them to be mirrored onto the asynchronous backend.
31-* `FolderAdapter`: Wraps a file system, and scopes all interactions to a subfolder of that file system.
32-* `Emscripten`: Lets you mount Emscripten file systems inside BrowserFS.
33-
34-More backends can be defined by separate libraries, so long as they extend the `BaseFileSystem` class. Multiple backends can be active at once at different locations in the directory hierarchy.
35-
36-For more information, see the [API documentation for BrowserFS](https://jvilk.com/browserfs/1.4.1/index.html).
